README.OSK -- PtyMan 1.3, as the author posted itReimer Mellin's pseudo-terminal file manager for OS-9/68000, version 1.3(RCS 1.3, 91/06/08), from its posting to comp.os.os9 and sub.sources.os9 on22 June 1991 (Volume 2, Issues 3-5): two parts of source and one ofbinaries.  The binaries in CMDS/DRIVERS are the author's own, decoded fromthat posting; each passes its module CRC.Changes: none to any file.  The shar was unpacked on a host and every lineending turned back into a CR; nothing else differs.Not tested.  This collection's emulator loads no file managers or drivers,so nothing here has been seen to work.  ptyman.doc says how it is used.Other copies that exist and are not here, for anyone who wants them:  - PtyMan 1.2.1.2 (1989), the source Microware's archive carries as    OSK_DRIVERS_SRC/ptys.lzh; an earlier release of this.  - A 1991 rebuild by Douglas Kemp (CERN) with a local path.h and a 1992    MM/1 build by Philip Brown (DRIVERS/ptynew.lzh, ptybin.lzh).  - Ilja Levinson's 1995 changes (DRIVERS/ptylev.zip): an EOF and a    backspace fix and mshell line-editing support, as diffs.lev.  They are    changes to Mellin's source, and his notice grants reproduction and    distribution but not modification, so they are left for the reader.  path.h in the later copies is Microware's DEFS/path.h with PtyMan's  fields added, and cannot be shipped; version 1.3 as posted does not  carry one.